A||||1||beer_stud_21||Distributor and timing questions.||||1||
Z||000000||beer_stud_21||04-07-2001||05:51 PM||||Hey all,<P>Well, I think im finally getting close to having my first running fiero.  I've got a couple questions for all you pro's.  <P>A) The distributor has that driveshaft coming out the bottom, when I pulled the distributor out this driveshaft practically fell off.  My question is:  Is this thing saposed to be held on somehow (a set screw or something) Im about to reinstall the distributor and am afraid of having this shaft fall down into the engine when I reinstall it.  <P>B) I didn't make any marks on the distributor when I pulled it.  Mostly because I just got the car and it hasn't run in about 3-4 years.  I didn't have the slightest idea how close the timing was and figured I was better off to set it myself than just put it back where it was.  My dad said he would help me set it.  He has been setting the timing on VW sawmill engines for 30 yrs.  Are there any tricks to it or pointers you can give us?  My dad says we dont even need a timing light really.  Just crank the engine manually till #1 cylinder is TDC, then point the rotor at #1cylinder.  After that you can fine tune it by twisting the dist housing with the engine running eh?  Let me know if this isn't a good idea. <P>Thanks everyone!  You are the reason I own a fiero.....<P>-Marlin<BR>85GT/auto  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||04-07-2001||07:26 PM||||You've got the right idea about setting the timing....do it that way.<BR>The shaft at the bottom of the dist just slides in the underside of the dist. Sometimes it comes out when you pull the dist, sometimes not...no biggie. Just slide it back in...it'll seat itself in the block/oil pump when you put it back in...nothing to worry about. Good luck! M7F ||||reg||1
